1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:01,490
C.

2
00:00:01,490 --> 00:00:07,090
Amy is talking with Millie about her problems in learning English.

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:10,940
Work in pairs and talk about the topic.

4
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:15,975
Use the conversation below as a model.

5
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:21,870
Millie, I'm really worried about my English.

6
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:24,110
Don't worry, Amy.

7
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:27,710
There are many ways to get better at English.

8
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:34,170
I think you can try listening to English as often as possible.

9
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:36,970
What should I listen to?

10
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:42,410
There are many online shows with people talking in English.

11
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:47,870
But remember, you don't have to understand every word.

12
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:52,940
Try to focus on the main idea of a talk or speech.

13
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:57,330
That's a good idea. What else?

14
00:00:57,330 --> 00:01:02,330
How about reading English aloud every morning?

15
00:01:02,330 --> 00:01:06,210
Try to pronounce each word correctly.

16
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:08,460
I'll have a try.

17
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:10,240
Thank you, Millie.
